# API Integration Patterns

## API Client Structure
All API clients MUST extend [BaseApi](mdc:src/api/base.api.ts):

```typescript
import { BaseApi } from "../../api/base.api";
import { Item, CreateDto, UpdateDto } from "./interfaces";

class FeatureApi extends BaseApi {
  constructor() {
    super("/endpoint"); // Backend endpoint
  }

  async getAll(filters?: Filters): Promise<Item[]> {
    const params = new URLSearchParams();
    if (filters?.status) params.append('status', filters.status);
    
    const query = params.toString();
    return this.get<Item[]>(query ? `?${query}` : "");
  }

  async getById(id: string): Promise<Item> {
    return this.get<Item>(`/${id}`);
  }

  async create(data: CreateDto): Promise<Item> {
    return this.post<Item, CreateDto>("", data);
  }

  async update(id: string, data: UpdateDto): Promise<Item> {
    return this.put<Item, UpdateDto>(`/${id}`, data);
  }

  async delete(id: string): Promise<void> {
    return this.delete<void>(`/${id}`);
  }
}

// Export singleton instance
export const featureApi = new FeatureApi();
```

## Backend API Mapping
- Base URL: `http://localhost:3000` (development)
- Authentication: JWT token in Authorization header (handled by BaseApi)
- Error handling: Automatic (handled by BaseApi)

## HTTP Methods
- `GET` - Fetch data
- `POST` - Create new resource
- `PUT` - Full update
- `PATCH` - Partial update
- `DELETE` - Remove resource

## Query Parameters
```typescript
// Build query params for filters
const params = new URLSearchParams();
if (status) params.append('status', status);
if (type) params.append('type', type);
const query = params.toString();
```

## Error Handling
BaseApi handles:
- 401 Unauthorized → Redirects to login
- 403 Forbidden → Shows error message
- 500 Server Error → Shows error message
- Network errors → Shows connection error

## Type Safety
Always provide TypeScript generics:
```typescript
return this.get<ReturnType>(`/path`);
return this.post<ReturnType, RequestType>(`/path`, data);
```
